}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfingering","abstract":[{"text":"Fingering is typically indicated 1,2,3,4,5. Multiple fingerings may be given, typically to substitute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fingerings in the middle of a note. The substitution and alternate values are “no” if the attribute is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present. For guitar and other fretted instruments, the fingering element represents the fretting finger; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pluck element represents the plucking finger.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFrame":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The frame type represents a frame or fretboard diagram used together with a chord symbol. The representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is based on the NIFF guitar grid with additional information. The frame type’s unplayed attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"what to display above a string that has no associated frame-note element. Typical values are x and the empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string. If the attribute is not present, the display of the unplayed string is application-defined."}],"title":"MXLFrame","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFrame"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFrame"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlframe","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFrame"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFret":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The fret element is used with tablature notation and chord diagrams. Fret numbers start with 0 for an open"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string and 1 for the first fret."}],"title":"MXLFret","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","